@startuml sd-amqp-event-propagation
skinparam style strictuml
autonumber
title SD - Create Route: CQRS command + AMQP event propagation (P2)

actor "Backoffice" as User
participant "RouteController\n(instance 1)" as Ctrl
participant "RouteService" as Svc
participant "RouteRepository\n(write model)" as RR
participant "RouteProjector" as Proj
participant "RouteReadRepository\n(read model)" as RM
participant "ReplicationOutbox" as Outbox
participant "AmqpReplicationPublisher" as Pub
participant "airports.events\n(fanout)" as Ex
participant "ReplicationEventConsumer\n(instance 2)" as Cons2
participant "RouteService\n(instance 2)" as Svc2

User -> Ctrl : POST /api/routes (CreateRouteDTO)
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Svc : createRoute(dto, isReplication=false)
activate Svc
note right of Svc : one @Transactional unit:\nwrite model + read model + outbox
Svc -> RR : save(route)
Svc -> Proj : project(route)
Proj -> RM : save(RouteReadModel)
Svc -> Outbox : enqueue(POST /api/routes, payload)
Outbox -> Outbox : save ReplicationTask(PENDING,\npeerUrl = "amqp://broker")
Svc --> Ctrl : RouteViewDTO
Ctrl --> User : 201 Created
deactivate Svc
deactivate Ctrl

== Background publisher (every 2 s) ==
Pub -> Pub : findTop100ByStatus(PENDING)
Pub -> Ex : publish persistent JSON envelope\n(eventType=ROUTE_CREATED,\nmessageId=<origin>-<taskId>)
Ex --> Pub : publisher confirm (<= 5 s)
Pub -> Pub : task.markDone()
note right of Pub : no confirm -> retry with backoff\nmin(60 s, 5*2^attempts), 10 attempts -> FAILED

== Broker fans out to every bound queue ==
Ex -> Cons2 : deliver from queue\nairports.events.airports-routes-2
activate Cons2
Cons2 -> Cons2 : originNodeId == own id?\nyes -> ignore (ack)
Cons2 -> Svc2 : createRoute(dto, isReplication=true)
activate Svc2
Svc2 -> Svc2 : idempotent apply\n(existing id -> return existing;\nlast-writer-wins by lastModified)
Svc2 -> Svc2 : save write model\n+ project() read model
Svc2 --> Cons2 : ok -> ack
deactivate Svc2
deactivate Cons2
note right of Cons2 : failure -> listener retry (3 attempts,\n1 s * 2) -> dead-letter queue (.dlq)
note over Ex : Flight Operations consumes the same event\nfrom its own queue (local copy of routes)
@enduml
